  title: The Sierra Madre is not a wall
  body: "The Sierra Madre weakens the winds of typhoons that cross it, by about 1\u201313%
    in one study. It does not block them, and their rain can fall even harder on
    its western side, so floods stay a danger. Its forests also hold the soil in
    place."
